-- title:
--   Γ₀(M')-layer lies in fractions of classify-values at the Tate point
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $M' \ge 1$ with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity for which there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((\mathfrak q))$ given by `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of `xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`, the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios $p_f/p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of two modular forms of the same weight on $\Gamma_H$ (with $p_g$-series nonzero), where $H = \ker\big((\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\big)$ is the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\ell$, $M'$ units in $A$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$; let $j \in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the $j$-series over $L$, assumed nonzero. Assume further: stability of level-$\ell$ structures in the sense of `IsLevelPStructure` (equations, vanishing of $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$ at both $x$-coordinates, invertibility of the two independence elements) under variable change, and stability of `IsGamma0PowAt` data under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on projective models of Weierstrass curves with invertible discriminant over $A$-algebras that is chord–tangent and has the origin as identity; a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; and the existence, for every $A$-algebra $T$, of graded homomorphisms of the projective-model rings realising variable changes (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and coefficient maps along $A$-algebra maps (`IsCoefficientHom`), compatibly with the irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be an absolute moduli package for the rigid datum `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q …`: a ring $B_0$ over $A$ with a universal point such that every point over an $A$-algebra $T$ is the image of the universal one under a unique $A$-algebra map, and write $\mathrm{classify}_x : B_0 \to K$ for the map attached to a point $x$ over $K$. Let $x$ be a point over $K$ of the associated moduli datum, whose classes consist of a Weierstrass curve with invertible discriminant together with a $\Gamma_0$-power tuple of kernel polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$, a level-$\ell$ structure, and a Drinfeld pair of $q$-sections, taken modulo variable change. Assume $\mathrm{jOf}(x)$ has Laurent expansion $j(\mathfrak q^{q\ell}) =$ `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`, and assume the hypothesis $h\mu$ pinning $x$ to the Tate point: there are a variable change $C$ over $L((\mathfrak q))$ and a raw representative $r$ of $x$ such that $C$ has $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$ and its unit $u$ satisfies $u\,(2X+1/6) = 2Y + X$ for $(X,Y)$ the toric cusp point `cuspPoint L (q*ℓ) ξ ![1,0]`; the curve of $r$ maps to $C \bullet \mathrm{Tate}$, the Tate curve over $L$ in the variable $\mathfrak q^{q\ell}$; for each prime $p \mid M'$ with $k = v_p(M')$, each field $F'$, ring map $f : L \to F'$ and primitive $p^k$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the $p$-component of the level tuple of $r$, pushed to $L((\mathfrak q))$ and then along $f$, is the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` twist by $C$ (mapped along $f$) in degree `gamma0PowDeg p k` of $\prod_{1 \le a \le p^k/2,\ p \nmid a} (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,(q\ell)\,\zeta^a)_1)$; the level-$\ell$ structure of $r$ maps to the $C$-twist of the Katz cusp data `cuspData L (q*ℓ) ξ ![q,0] ![0,-q]`; and there are $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ with Laurent expansions the four coordinates of the $C$-twist of `cuspData L (q*ℓ) ξ ![ℓ,0] ![0,-ℓ]` through which the two Drinfeld sections of $r$ pass in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`. Then for every $g \in L((\mathfrak q))$ belonging to the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-field of $q$-expansion ratios for $\Gamma_0(M')$, and every $k \in K$ whose Laurent expansion is $g$ with $\mathfrak q$ replaced by $\mathfrak q^{q\ell}$, there exist $a, b \in B_0$ with $\mathrm{classify}_x(b) \ne 0$ and $k \cdot \mathrm{classify}_x(b) = \mathrm{classify}_x(a)$.
--
--   The statement says that, at the Tate point of the rigidified moduli problem with $\Gamma_0(M')$-power, level-$\ell$ and Drinfeld $q$-level data, the $\Gamma_0(M')$-layer of the $q$-expansion function field (read in the variable $\mathfrak q^{q\ell}$) lies inside the fraction field of the image of the classifying homomorphism $B_0 \to K$. It feeds the density statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.dense_range_classify_of_muTuple_pin_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.dense_range_classify_of_muTuple_pin_gamma0Pow), which identifies the function field cut out by the moduli package with the modular function field of the relevant level.
